  "result": "**Gate verdict: OK** (first run; 1 of 6 used).\n\n**Body** — `library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/standstill.lean`:\n\n```lean\ndef body : Formula :=\n  .cmp (.measure \"kin_speed\" [aU]) .le pSpeedTolerance\n```\n\nOne comparison over the track formal `u` and the parameter `speed_tolerance`, reading the single claimed atom `kin.speed`. `.le` because the contract says \"at most\" and glosses it \"at or below\". No window, no region, no control-state atom — the contract's exclusion list rules all of them out — and an unobserved speed leaves the comparison unknown, which is what `blind` turns on.\n\nI checked `Core/Language/Semantics.lean:274` (`\"kin_speed\", [x]`) rather than guessing arity from the maximal `[t, none, none]` row in `atomArgSorts`.\n\n**Witnesses** — one instance with `speed_tolerance` = 0.2 m/s (`Units.micrometresPerSecond 200000`; the integer `metresPerSecond` constructor cannot express it), one car as track 1 and a 10 m square intersection for the junction the narratives name:\n\n- `holds`: at rest at (0, −6) m, speed 0 at all three observations → compliant\n- `fails`: rolling north at 2 m/s → violated\n- `blind`: the same approach with `kin.speed` masked → unknown\n\n**Narrowings: none.** The contract fixed the quantity, the strictness of the bound and the fact that the magnitude comes from the caller, so no choice was left open in the body; every figure I chose lives in the witness file. The record needed no repair, and no dependency defect was possible (the catalogue is empty).\n\n`task_result.md` is written at `/local-scratch2/sma407/scratch_core/launch/remote/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/results/demo22-1109-0108/iter-001/code/concept__drv_motion_standstill/task_result.md`.",
